Step 1: Create Role-Specific Pre-Approved Tables
In the Supabase SQL Editor, create separate whitelist tables (pre_approved_admins, pre_approved_academic_heads, and pre_approved_system_admins) to store pre-authorized staff credentials securely.

We will open the SQL Editor in your Supabase dashboard and run a SQL script to create three tables: pre_approved_admins, pre_approved_academic_heads, and pre_approved_system_admins.
Each of these tables will be structured with the exact same columns needed for your whitelist check: initials, firstname, surname, email, phone, role, and temppass. This allows your backend to verify activation details securely before a user signs up.

