Step 3: Enable Strict RLS and Keep Tables Private
Keep Row Level Security (RLS) enabled on all tables without granting any public/anonymous read policies, ensuring raw whitelist data cannot be queried directly from the frontend.

We will open the SQL Editor in your Supabase dashboard and run a SQL script to enable Row Level Security (RLS) on all six of our tables (pre_approved_admins, pre_approved_academic_heads, pre_approved_system_admins, admins, academic_heads, and system_admins).
Each of these tables will have strict security enforced without granting any public or anonymous read policies. This ensures that raw whitelist credentials and private personnel records cannot be queried or accessed directly from the frontend by unauthenticated users.

